From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lun Dong <lundong@google.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [RISCV] Add Zvt matrix extension support

The RISC-V backend does not know about the CoralNPU Zvt matrix
extension, so its tile configuration and matrix multiply instructions
cannot be assembled and the vector configuration around them is not
tracked.

Add:
- Subtarget features Zvtbase, Zvt8e, Zvt16e, Zvt64e, Zvti8i32mm,
  Zvtf8f32mm, Zvtf16f32mm and Zvtf32f32mm.
- Instruction and encoding definitions in RISCVInstrInfoZvt.td for tile
  configuration (msetmtype, msettm, msettn, msettk), tile load/store
  (vtle*, vtse*), tile move (vtmv.v.t, vtmv.t.v), vtzero, vtdiscard and
  the matrix multiplies (vtmms.tvv, vtmmu.tvv, vtfmm.tvv,
  vtfmm.alt.tvv).
- Intrinsic declarations in IntrinsicsRISCVZvt.td and the corresponding
  ISel patterns.
- Knowledge of the Zvt pseudos in the VSETVLI insertion and analysis
  passes, so the SEW/LMUL they require is taken into account.
